## 🛡️ Best Practices to Prevent Future Compromise

| Action | How to Implement |
|-------|------------------|
| **Enforce Strong Passwords** | Use Zimbra COS (Class of Service) to set password policy: min length, complexity, expiry |
| **Disable Legacy Auth** | Block IMAP/POP if not needed; force modern auth |
| **Monitor Logs Weekly** | Run Step 1 manually every Monday |
| **Use Fail2Ban** | Install `fail2ban` to auto-block IPs after repeated login failures |
| **Keep Zimbra Updated** | Patch monthly: `sudo su - zimbra -c "zmupdate"` |
| **Educate Users** | Warn about phishing; never share passwords |

### Quick Fail2Ban Setup (Optional):
```bash
sudo apt install fail2ban
sudo cp /etc/fail2ban/jail.conf /etc/fail2ban/jail.local
# Then add Zimbra auth log to monitor
```

